mud-builder-server is the only component that touches the MUD's files: an Express API (port 61000, pattern-matched to kingdom-tactics-server) over C:\Projects\merc-mud\2.4\area. Its central invariant is the write gate: unless MUD_WRITE_ENABLED=true (set by the experimental compose deployment, or deliberately for staging E2E), every disk-writing route (PUT save, POST /api/reload) returns 403 and the tool is preview/download-only. Saves are emit-validated (model must re-parse), atomic (temp+rename), and always preceded by a timestamped backup under area/backups/. Reload requests write sentinel files (reload.signal with the area name for the zero-downtime in-place reload; copyover.signal for the fresh-slate warm reboot) that merc-mud's update_handler consumes once per second. Errors never escape a route handler; expected failures are 4xx JSON.
